{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1010312-conquering-heroes-in-proofing","id":1010312,"title":"Conquering Heroes in Proofing","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-30T12:44:08-08:00","id":1010312,"title":"Conquering Heroes in Proofing","content":"So... I noticed this on the Monday meeting notes and where its currently at. <br /> <br /> Has there been any talk as to what this book goes into? I'm hazarding a guess its more detail about Heroes, but I'm wondering if there's anything more to it? <br /> <br /> All I've heard about it so far is its title, so any info people might have to share would be wonderful. ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T12:46:19-08:00","id":1010314,"title":"","content":"It's Night Horrors for Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T13:03:29-08:00","id":1010317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1010312-conquering-heroes-in-proofing?p=1010314#post1010314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's Night Horrors for Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking over some of the other example books... They seem kind of all over the place as to what they provide. Mostly example antagonists... The Unbidden seems to talk about how Mage can better be a horror game, which sounds very useful and evocative... But also seems to be an opportunity to provide more supernatural powers that the PCs can have? <br /> <br /> What do you think or hope Conquering Heroes will provide? <br /> <br /> And has anyone working on it talked some about it beyond that its a Night Horrors book? I went searching through the Onyx Path blogs and couldn't find any mention of it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T13:14:18-08:00","id":1010322,"title":"","content":"It's currently the fourth item listed on the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/schedule\" target=\"_blank\">Schedule</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T13:28:32-08:00","id":1010324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1010312-conquering-heroes-in-proofing?p=1010322#post1010322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's currently the fourth item listed on the <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://theonyxpath.com/schedule&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Schedule</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually just found that after some googling and was coming here to post that! You beat me to the punch there though. ^^<br /> <br /> So it says: &quot;BTP \u2013 Night Horrors: Conquering Heroes: This antagonist book for Beast: The Primordial features examples of Heroes, as well as Beasts that have undergone their Inheritance and become lurking monsters or terrifying supernatural forces-to-be-reckoned with. Because Beast has a focus on crossover, some vampire, werewolves, mages, etc. will be included and described in story terms. 128 pages. PDF/PoD.&quot;<br /> <br /> It looks to mostly be a bestiary type book, I guess... I like having some more presence of other Beasts who have undergone their Inheritance as being a source of Antagonists. I think there needs to be something that can threaten a Lair and one of the Unfettered might be a good candidate for such threats... <br /> <br /> I like the idea of presenting other supernatural monsters in story terms. I'm interested in better seeing how Beasts and their Kin can clash. <br /> <br /> More information on Heroes, but that's to be expected... Can't say that really excites me, but I'm hoping the book helps make Heroes more interesting to me. <br /> <br /> It's not mentioned, but I hope there's more description of the Primordial Dream as a place of nightmares and horror. <br /> <br /> Anything in particular that catches your interest?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T13:45:13-08:00","id":1010331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1010312-conquering-heroes-in-proofing?p=1010324#post1010324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything in particular that catches your interest?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Night Horrors books are pretty uniformly antagonist books whose primary utility beyond specific characters to transplant into your game is as a collection of examples of how the gameline's metaphysics can get uniquely weird \u2014 the Strix and the Idigam got their debut as mechanically-modeled modern concerns in Wicked Dead and Wolfsbane, to give more broadly applicable examples, but from a worldbuilding perspective the salient elements are likely going to be strange template mutations and a handful of new widgets with varying levels of acquisition-readiness.<br /> <br /> I look forward to it for the reasons I look forward to reading any given &quot;collection of example phenomena&quot; book, but I'm not banking on game-changing material being in here rather than in the PG or the STG. I consume voraciously, but I'd be lying if I said I expected big setting implications to be gotten without putting the pieces together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T13:53:48-08:00","id":1010333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1010312-conquering-heroes-in-proofing?p=1010331#post1010331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Night Horrors books are pretty uniformly antagonist books whose primary utility beyond specific characters to transplant into your game is as a collection of examples of how the gameline's metaphysics can get uniquely weird \u2014 the Strix and the Idigam got their debut as mechanically-modeled modern concerns in Wicked Dead and Wolfsbane, to give more broadly applicable examples, but from a worldbuilding perspective the salient elements are likely going to be strange template mutations and a handful of new widgets with varying levels of acquisition-readiness.<br /> <br /> I look forward to it for the reasons I look forward to reading any given &amp;quot;collection of example phenomena&amp;quot; book, but I'm not banking on game-changing material being in here rather than in the PG or the STG. I consume voraciously, but I'd be lying if I said I expected big setting implications to be gotten without putting the pieces together.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fair approach for it, I have to admit. <br /> <br /> I guess what I'm most looking forward to then is some insight into other antagonists for Beasts beyond Heroes. I think that's something I could use some help on for better fleshing out threats. Most of what I can think of involves Heroes, other Beasts regarding territory disputes, and largely gaining antagonists vicariously through the supernatural beings they share Kinship with. <br /> <br /> ... I could definitely do with a book to help broaden my horizons regarding antagonists for Beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T15:48:51-08:00","id":1010850,"title":"","content":"I hope there's some new types of antagonists rather than just pre-statted up existing creatures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T16:41:43-08:00","id":1010868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1010312-conquering-heroes-in-proofing?p=1010850#post1010850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope there's some new types of antagonists rather than just pre-statted up existing creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that would be nice, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T19:58:13-08:00","id":1010913,"title":"","content":"Considering Beasts thing with family I'm kind of curious if anything more will be brought up on how kinship works with some of these entities. Like a Beast can't be kin with one of the unchained, but how many monsters might fall under the category of being kin in theory, but in practice it doesn't happen for reasons x,y, and z.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T03:45:29-08:00","id":1010999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1010312-conquering-heroes-in-proofing?p=1010913#post1010913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering Beasts thing with family I'm kind of curious if anything more will be brought up on how kinship works with some of these entities. Like a Beast can't be kin with one of the unchained, but how many monsters might fall under the category of being kin in theory, but in practice it doesn't happen for reasons x,y, and z.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dave mentioned Abyssal entities are not Kin, period. I don't remember if this was an oversight in the Beast book or a retcon. I do remember people arguing over whether Abyssals do count as Kin or not.<br /> <br /> I think Abyssals are a case of &quot;They are Kin. Except when they aren't. Or both. Or none.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T07:08:07-08:00","id":1011064,"title":"","content":"It also includes something called the Insatiate. (Or Insatiable maybe.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T07:17:02-08:00","id":1011066,"title":"","content":"Well that would imply Beasts who <i>can't </i>sate their Hunger. Something eternally hungry that would make Beasts balk at its sheer indulgence.<br /> <br /> That... does not sound like anything I'd want to get in the way of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T07:32:45-08:00","id":1011071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1010312-conquering-heroes-in-proofing?p=1011066#post1011066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well that would imply Beasts who <i>can't </i>sate their Hunger. Something eternally hungry that would make Beasts balk at its sheer indulgence.<br /> <br /> That... does not sound like anything I'd want to get in the way of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a sensible reaction to me, considering that satiable Beasts are capable of laying waste to lives left, right and centre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode